#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.024pt, 85.32pt, "stage disease diagnostics. In this context, the DNA Origami technique, with its high ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 103.46pt, "addressability, enables both the assembly of plasmonic nanostructures with nanometric ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 121.46pt, "accuracy, and the deterministic placement of a single analyte molecule precisely at the ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 139.58pt, "generated hotspot within them. To date, most DNA Origami based nanoantennas rely on ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 157.58pt, "gold or silver nanoparticles (NPs), whose plasmonic resonances are confined to the visible ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 175.7pt, "spectrum, severely limiting their use in other spectral ranges. To extend the operating ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 193.7pt, "range, we have recently established a robust strategy for self-assembling programmable ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 211.82pt, "ultraviolet (UV)-plasmonic dimer antennas using rhodium nanocubes. Herein, we ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 229.94pt, "leverage this tailored architecture to systematically investigate its performance for single-")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 247.94pt, "molecule UV-SERS. We demonstrated how biofabricated Rh-dimers can be used to detect ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 266.06pt, "the characteristic SERS signal of a single streptavidin molecule linked at the dimer’s gap. ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 284.09pt, "Our results are validated through polarization dependent measurements that yield the ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 302.21pt, "expected signal modulation depending on the the dimer orientation only for the DNA ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 320.33pt, "origami with a protein at the hotspot. This work establishes a highly sensitive and ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 338.33pt, "polarization-tunable UV-SERS platform, laying a solid foundation for label-free optical ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 356.45pt, "investigation and bio-spectroscopy of individual biomolecules in the UV spectral range. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 14.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.024pt, 415.85pt, "Introduction ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.024pt, 447.77pt, "Surface-enhanced Raman scattering (SERS) provides non-destructive, label-free ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 465.79pt, "molecular fingerprinting with high-sensitivity, offering a deep understanding of ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 483.91pt, "biomolecular structure and dynamics")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(274.73pt, 479.35pt, "1–7")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(286.85pt, 483.91pt, ". This technique relies critically on nanoscale ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 502.03pt, "plasmonic hotspots that generate enhanced localized electromagnetic fields, a mechanism ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 520.03pt, "that has enabled the use of Raman spectroscopy for single-molecule detection")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(464.02pt, 515.47pt, "8–10")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(480.1pt, 520.03pt, ". So far, ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 538.15pt, "diverse SERS platforms have been extensively reported")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(375.91pt, 533.59pt, "11")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(384.07pt, 538.15pt, ", with examples based on ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 556.15pt, "colloidal nanoparticles (NPs)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(247.01pt, 551.59pt, "12")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(255.17pt, 556.15pt, ", nanoporous systems")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(375.07pt, 551.59pt, "13")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(383.11pt, 556.15pt, ", and nanostructures or ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 574.27pt, "nanoantennas prepared via different lithographic methods")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(365.83pt, 569.71pt, "14")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(373.99pt, 574.27pt, ". In general, conventional top-")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 592.39pt, "down fabrication methods often lacks nanometric precision and reproducibility to ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 610.39pt, "assemble hotspots with consistent and enhanced optical properties even for homogeneous ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 628.51pt, "substrates")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(137.3pt, 623.95pt, "13,15,16")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(165.5pt, 628.51pt, ". Furthermore, with these techniques it is extremely challenging to ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 646.51pt, "deterministically position an individual analyte within the hotspot.   ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 664.66pt, "To overcome these limitations, biofabrication based on DNA origami")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(428.83pt, 660.1pt, "3,17,18")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(452.86pt, 664.66pt, " has emerged ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 682.66pt, "as a powerful bottom-up assembly strategy by assembling functionalized nanoparticles ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 700.78pt, "with synthetic oligonucleotides into nanometric plasmonic structures")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(419.11pt, 696.22pt, "19–22")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(439.39pt, 700.78pt, ". In addition, the ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 718.9pt, "same addressable DNA scaffold can host a single target molecule directly within the ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 736.9pt, "nanogap")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(130.58pt, 732.34pt, "23")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(138.74pt, 736.9pt, ", fulfilling both requirements for reliable single-molecule SERS. For instance, ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 755.016pt, "Kosti Tapio et al. reported a method for utilizing DNA origami to precisely position single ")
