  #line-at(90.024pt, 150.62pt, "Figure 1a depicts the strategy to fabricate Rh NC dimers with an average interparticle ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 168.62pt, "distance of 10.7 ± 3.2 nm using the DNA origami technique. In brief, a rectangular DNA ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 186.74pt, "origami with dimensions of 180 nm × 5 nm × 15 nm (length × height × width) and a 8.5 ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 204.86pt, "nm wide ‘mast’ at the center is modified to incorporate through DNA hybridization two ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 222.86pt, "Rh NCs. At the dimer hotspot, which coincides with the upper part of the mast, a biotin ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 240.98pt, "modification enables the incorporation of a single streptavidin protein. This approach ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 258.98pt, "enables the fabrication of UV antennas based on Rh NC dimers with and without a single ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 277.13pt, "protein at the hotspot for control measurements. Further details on the DNA origami and ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 295.25pt, "the incorporation of Rh NCs and the single streptavidin can be found in previous works")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(506.5pt, 290.69pt, "39")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(514.66pt, 295.25pt, ". ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 313.25pt, "Figures 1b includes a TEM image of the dimer structures, while additional TEM ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 331.37pt, "micrographs are reported in Supporting Information (SI – note#1). Two sets of Rh NCs ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 349.37pt, "have been considered, with size of 19 and 24 nm, respectively. The UV/Vis extinction ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 367.49pt, "measurements revealed a broad resonance centered between 300 and 320 nm in buffer ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 385.49pt, "conditions, respectively for 19nm and 24 nm Rh NCs (see SI – note#2).  ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 411.65pt, "SERS measurements were performed using two excitation wavelengths. First, to probe ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 429.65pt, "the response of Rh NC dimers near their absorbance maximum, a 325 nm laser was ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 447.77pt, "coupled to a HORIBA Raman system capable of acquiring spectroscopic 2D maps and ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 465.79pt, "equipped with an ultraviolet polarizer in the optical path, as schematically shown in Fig. ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 483.91pt, "S3 (SI). Second, for comparison with the most commonly used excitation wavelength in ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 502.03pt, "UV-SERS, the nanostructures were investigated using a different setup (not capable of 2D ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 520.03pt, "mapping) coupled to a 266 nm laser and equipped with a half-wave plate to rotate the ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 538.15pt, "incident polarization (see Fig. S4, SI). The use of this second excitation wavelength allows ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 556.15pt, "probing single molecules at energies closer to the absorption bands of several aromatic ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 574.27pt, "amino acids, which exhibit characteristic absorption features at approximately 255 nm, ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 592.39pt, "270 nm, and 286 nm, thereby enhancing the contribution of molecular UV absorbance.")
