  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(238.01pt, 91.1pt, "directly validates the coupling between the external optical ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 116.54pt, "field and the engineered plasmonic mode of the dimer, transforming the structure from a ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 134.66pt, "passive amplifier into an active optical element. ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 152.66pt, "These capabilities are fundamentally enabled by a synergistic plasmonic cavity. Our ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 170.78pt, "micropatterned control experiments offer visual proof that the aluminum film substrate is ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 188.78pt, "indispensable, actively contributing to the enhancement rather than serving as a passive ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 206.9pt, "support. This synergy among material (Rh), geometry (dimer), and substrate (Al) forms ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 224.9pt, "the core of our platform's performance. ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 243.02pt, "Looking forward, the inherent programmability of DNA origami provides a clear path for ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 261.14pt, "advancement. The scaffold can be redesigned to tune the nanoantenna's spectral response ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 279.17pt, "or to present multiple probes for multiplexed detection. The proven polarization control ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 297.29pt, "further suggests promising routes toward developing chiral plasmonic sensors. While ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 315.29pt, "challenges remain in areas like large-scale uniformity and absolute enhancement factor ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 333.41pt, "quantification, this work decisively extends the reach of DNA-assembled plasmonics into ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 351.53pt, "the UV regime. It lays a versatile foundation for applications demanding label-free, single-")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 369.53pt, "molecule spectral fingerprinting with built-in optical tunability, from fundamental bio-")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 387.65pt, "spectroscopy to next-generation sensing. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 14.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.024pt, 421.01pt, "Methods ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.024pt, 452.93pt, "Rhodium nanoparticles synthesis ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.024pt, 478.75pt, "Rhodium nanocubes were synthesized using a seed-mediated polyol method following Zhang et ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 496.75pt, "al. (Size-Tunable Rhodium Nanostructures for Wavelength-Tunable Ultraviolet Plasmonics, ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 514.87pt, "Nanoscale Horizons, 2015). Potassium bromide and polyvinylpyrrolidone were used as shape-")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 532.99pt, "directing and stabilizing agents, with ethylene glycol acting as solvent and reducing agent. Seed ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 550.99pt, "particles were first prepared at 160 °C, followed by a controlled growth step via injection of a ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 569.11pt, "rhodium precursor into the seed solution. The reaction was maintained at 160 °C and then cooled ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 587.11pt, "to room temperature, yielding rhodium nanocubes with average edge lengths of approximately 24 ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 605.23pt, "and 40 nm. After synthesis, the nanocubes were washed and redispersed in deionized water. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.024pt, 631.51pt, "Assembly of DNA Origami “Boat” ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.024pt, 657.34pt, "DNA origami structures were assembled from a 7249-nt M13mp18 scaffold using 243 staple ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 675.46pt, "strands in 1× TAE buffer supplemented with 12 mM MgCl₂ (pH 8), following the protocol ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 693.58pt, "described in DNA-Origami-Assembled Rhodium Nanoantennas for Deep-UV Label-Free Single-")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 711.58pt, "Protein Detection (Corduri et al.). Staples were added in 10-fold excess over the scaffold (100-")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 729.7pt, "fold for functional staples). The mixture was thermally annealed from 70 °C to 25 °C. Purification ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 747.696pt, "was performed either by agarose gel electrophoresis or by Amicon ultrafiltration. Streptavidin was ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 765.816pt, "subsequently added in 20-fold excess, incubated at room temperature, and the final constructs ")
]

